{
  "$comment": "Shared test vectors for the CK-12 scope of the B2 `media_refs` field (decision 0003 #16; checker design, CK-12). Sources: the guide's decision on issue #232 (https://github.com/narenccode/learnops/issues/232#issuecomment-7176861868), item 6, and the M1 scope confirmation and review by Akshita on the same issue (https://github.com/narenccode/learnops/issues/232#issuecomment-7183976351), which asks for the cases marked 'm1-scope-confirmed'. The guide's decision: the embedded-media scope listed on that issue is the v1 definition; data: URIs are not flagged in v1; ordinary links, PDFs and iframes are not checked in v1; one shared extractor in the FR-C-01 model builder, which Course Studio reuses. Pure data: no code. Each case gives the text of one activity body ('format' markdown or html; 'input_kind' package or mbz, where an .mbz body is the HTML as the builder reads it) and what an extractor must produce and CK-12 must report. 'expected.media_refs' is the exact list of in-scope embedded-media references found, as written, in document order: every in-scope reference is listed, whether it is a full URL, a protocol-relative URL, a relative path, a Moodle @@PLUGINFILE@@/... reference or a data: URI, and each URL of an srcset is its own entry without its descriptor; an excluded construct (an ordinary link, a PDF link or an iframe) is not listed. 'expected.ck12_flagged' is the part of that list CK-12 reports as a full fixed URL: http://, https:// or a protocol-relative //host/ reference (the guide's list; checker design, CK-12). A Moodle @@PLUGINFILE@@/... reference, a relative path and a data: URI are not flagged. A null means the decision does not settle that part: a test must assert nothing about a null field. Status 'derived': follows directly from the guide's scope. Status 'm1-scope-confirmed': follows from Akshita's confirmation of the scope on issue #232 and her reading that media_refs lists every in-scope reference, which the guide's text does not state in so many words (the guide decided only that data: URIs are not flagged and that @@PLUGINFILE@@ paths pass). It is not a formal approval: that is given on the pull request, and these cases need the guide's agreement or Akshita's approval there. Status 'open-point': records a point that is not decided and asserts nothing about the undecided part. In the open-point case the ftp: reference is listed because that follows Akshita's listing interpretation (the same one as for data: and relative paths); only its CK-12 flagging is undecided, so only ck12_flagged is null. Open point: whether CK-12 flags a URI scheme other than http:, https: and data: (for example ftp: or file:). The guide's list names http://, https:// and //host/; Akshita proposes flagging any scheme other than data:, or else writing the other schemes as 'not checked in v1'. Not covered because the decisions do not say: attribute and tag case, quoting styles, Markdown image titles, duplicate references, unescaping of XML in .mbz content, and an img nested in a link. The scope names 'audio' and 'track' with the attribute src, as in the guide's listing; the checker design's CK-12 row names them without attributes. These vectors are not an extractor and there is no test-only extractor: the model-builder extractor (FR-C-01, Release 1) must pass them, and Course Studio reuses that extractor. Approval of the B2 contract change by the affected M1 owner is tracked separately, not in this file.",
